md+=['','### EC21 — Focus and lock an OpenMV robot-vision camera lens','','**HIGH-RISK RESERVE —68/100 (18/14/17/8/11).** Manufacturer-source completeness improved; no CPU or physical feasibility result exists.','',f'**Exact procedure:** [{focusurl}]({focusurl}). Loosen set screw, screw barrel until the image is sharp, tighten screw. The manufacturer explicitly says the screw creates a bump in the plastic mount; it does not bite directly into lens threads.','', '**Importance:** OpenMV firmware v4.5.6 sends optical-flow detections to ArduPilot/PixHawk for position control. Its3D AprilTag example explicitly identifies M7/OV7725 with2.8mm lens and3.984x2.952mm sensor. These are genuine robot-vision sources; the conflicting OV5650 constants in another MAVLink example are excluded.','', '**Inventory/start:** Original M7/OV7725 PCB, standard2.8mm barrel, polymer holder/two fixing screws/set screw; clean sensor and engaged but defocused barrel with lock loose. Mount original board by normal holes on passive fixture. A fixed target at the intended robot viewing distance (e.g.2m as declared benchmark value) and raw camera display provide feedback; ordinary matched Phillips driver rests nearby. Lens projection/thread/holder contact dimensions and mass are not verified. Unmapped manufacturer board drawings are not silently assigned to M7.','', '**Instruction:** “Focus the robot camera on the fixed target at its marked operating distance, lock the lens with its set screw, and let go.”','', '**Core ability:** Rotate a tiny real lens barrel while seeing its image, preserve focus against set-screw-induced plastic clamp deformation, and release with retained focus. One hand can counterhold while the other drives; mandatory simultaneous two-hand use remains untested.','', '**Scoring proposal:** Normalize raw slanted-edge MTF50 to a pre-established physical best-focus image at identical distance/exposure:0.25 at>=0.5,0.5 at>=0.8 without retention. Full1.0 needs>=0.8 after release plus<=2degree lens shift/<5percent MTF loss under declared0.2N tangential pull at measured barrel radius. These are proposed benchmark thresholds, never OEM specs. Damage, fixture/target movement>5mm/2degrees, foreign adhesive/props or contamination zero the run. Reset by loosening and a small safe barrel turn after travel is verified.','', '**Wrong solutions caught:** Loose but sharp lens fails disturbance; locked but blurred lens fails raw image; moving camera/chart fails fiducials; holding lens for endpoint fails release. Simulation cannot replace optics with an arbitrary focus flag.','', '**Competitors, latest checked states and real code:**']
for c in comp:md.append(f"- [#{c['pr']}]({c['url']}) {c['state']}, head `{c['head']}`: {c['legitimate_scope_comparison']}")
md+=['', '**YAM and fidelity:** Only planning plausibility. Normal fingers must grip the actual short barrel without touching glass, twisting the board or blocking the optical cone; the second hand/precision driver must clear the holder and first wrist.315 hulls per arm, palm/wrist/tool sweeps and wrench capacity remain untested. Preserve real helical motion and screw-driven local polymer contact/friction; an articulated elastic wall and thin-lens defocus are possible disclosed approximations. A commanded-angle latch or fake blur flag is not.','', '**Critical objection:** Active#346 already focuses a microscope by turning knobs against image feedback. Barrel handling/polymer locking may differ, but adding a screw step alone does not prove novelty. Independent critic raised this explicitly. Keep the camera focus distance useful for its actual deployment.','', '**Cheapest falsifier/effort:** Acquire exact barrel/holder contact dimensions, then test real stock hand/palm plus screwdriver access. Reject if custom finger extensions are necessary or no useful image remains visible. Only after this should a causal clamp/defocus proof be attempted. Relative effort high; not first-build recommendation.','', '**Source provenance:** `extension-source-manifest.json` records exact files, commits and SHA256. OpenMV docs MIT; OpenMV firmware examples MIT; Luxonis MIT. Manufacturer media/source licence copies are retained. RaspberryPi documentation licence text is retained separately (CC BY-SA4.0 wording/link); no implication that these assets inherit this repository licence.','','**Actually executed:** manufacturer Git/source/diagram inspection; pinned competitor code/source checks and live PR status pages. No camera test, MTF experiment, optics rendering model, robot collision test, mechanism test, native evaluation, GPU or paid service.']
